      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "The corrected construction newly names the compact clipping endpoints \\(\\kappa_-\\) and \\(\\kappa_+\\), so its complete post-image must add their symbol dependencies while preserving the original inputs.",
        "correct: The raw logarithms and empirical mark law were undefined when a tail count was zero, and the raw tail-index ratio need not lie in \\((1,2)\\) at finite \\(n\\).  Positive truncation, compact projection, and an empty-set fallback make the construction a total map without changing it on the probability-one asymptotic event used by the theorem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "def:local-linear-one-step",
      "change": "changed",
      "fields": [
        "construction"
      ],
      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "correct: The original construction did not specify a value on singular binwise Gram events.  A deterministic fallback makes the estimator a total sample map and is inactive on the uniformly vanishing failure event proved here."
      ]
    }
